{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G4sVXuKu9z8TMkpTg59URj","type":"tool_result","content":"Saved E08.1 = no. Next: E08.2 — Authorization at the action uses the original subject and the current actor, and earlier actors in the delegation chain never add access.\n  How to verify: 1) Open authorization code for delegated actions. 2) Check it decides on the original subject and the current actor. 3) Answer no if it grants access because of any earlier actor in the chain (nested `act` claims, parent identity) or a union of chain permissions.\nSaved E08.2 = unknown. Next: E08.3 — An action the parent was denied is also denied when routed through a more powerful peer, unless it carries its own explicit approval.\n  How to verify: 1) Find how a parent asks a peer or child to act. 2) Check the request carries the parent's limits and the peer re-checks them, or requires its own explicit approval. 3) Answer no if a peer acts with its own wider permissions on a parent's request without that check.\nSaved E08.3 = unknown. Next: E08.4 — Downstream services reject the parent's token when the child presents it (audience-bound tokens).\n  How to verify: 1) Find how child tokens are issued and how downstream services validate tokens. 2) Check tokens are audience-bound and services verify `aud`. 3) Answer no if audience is unset, a wildcard, or not checked. Answer unknown if downstream services are outside this repo.\nSaved E08.4 = unknown. Next: finish item E08 with `answer.py ... item E08 --rating ...`\nAdded red flag to E08.\nSaved pre-scan H005 = dismissed.\nSaved item E08 = gap. Next: E09.1 — A stop signal from the root reaches every descendant: nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks.\n  How to verify: 1) Find the stop handler. 2) Check it reaches nested children, remote workers, queued jobs, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks (cancel calls, MCP `notifications/cancelled`). 