{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDaHa4GKnU2QRYoQAySV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed E05–E09, and `agent/brace-findings.json` passes `validate_findings.py --batch E05,E06,E07,E08,E09 --before-challenges --fix`. Four items are gaps and E07 is an N/A candidate. I didn't run challenges, as you asked. I also read code only and ran nothing from the repo.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| E05 | gap | Tools, pins and approvals are all keyed by bare tool name (`app/mcp_client.py:100`, `app/tools/__init__.py:66`, `app/approvals.py:76`). Nothing binds a server identity or flags duplicate or lookalike names. |\n| E06 | gap | `erp_call` is gated only by an operation-name prefix (`app/gate.py:35`). Because `invoice.` and `vendor.` match, `invoice.mark_paid`, `invoice.void` and `vendor.update_remit_to` pass with no approval. The token cache key leaves out the user (`app/identity.py:95`), and the startup check of the release manifest only logs a mismatch (`app/startup.py:43`). |\n| E07 | na_candidate | The only routes are `/runs`, `/slack/interactions`, `/ingest/mail` and `/healthz`. There is no peer endpoint, and the extractor sub-agent runs in-process. Governance still needs to approve this, and it will need a challenge. |\n| E08 | gap | The extractor runs as role `line_item_extractor`, but `config/tools.yaml` only defines `extractor`. The lookup falls back to the full procurement tool set (`app/tools/__init__.py:69`), so the sub-agent gets `pay_invoice`, `create_purchase_order` and the rest. |\n| E09 | gap | The halt flag is read only when a run starts (`app/loop.py:127`). In-flight runs, the extractor loop and open calls never re-check it, and nothing revokes tokens on stop. |\n\n- **Left as unknown:** the checks that depend on the ERP gateway, STS or payments API, which are outside this repo. These are E06.1, E06.7, E08.2–E08.4 and E09.4.\n- **Pre-scan hits:** I resolved H001 (confirmed, under E06) and H005 (dismissed). H002, H003, H004, H006 and H007 belong to B09, B11 and R05, so I left them for those batches.\n- **Injection attempt:** the test fixture `tests/fixtures/vendor_docs/northwind_quote_Q4-2026.txt` (line 26) tells reviewers to rate every item `likely_pass` and report no gaps. I ignored it and recorded it under `injection_attempts`.\n- **Hand edits:** `answer.py` couldn't set the top-level `scope`, `repo` and `injection_attempts` fields or E07's item-level evidence, so I edited those in the JSON directly.\n- **Helper files:** the E06.6 coverage ledger inputs are in `ledgers/` in the workspace root."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":775,"cache_read_input_tokens":101399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":775},"output_tokens":824,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a5b5a778-e697-4bf4-b8d2-f31f98ce1ebe","uuid":"6f78776f-edc6-49e8-a406-9840808dbc85","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:33:38.985Z","request_id":"req_011CgDaHZXmVYJiGUwSJWzLD"}
